F-0229 reproduction — gate-budget-false-unavailable
dev, 2026-08-18, task T-BRANDOPEN-0817.
Machine: the project's own Windows host. Nothing else of mine was running.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
0. THE FILE THE RECORD NAMES DOES NOT EXIST IN THIS PROJECT
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The ledger says `where: .proof-os/gates/build.node.sh:44`. There is no
`build.node.sh` under .proof-os/gates/. The only copies are the read-only synced
plugin ones (.proof-os/.runtime/{proof-os,os042,claude-home/...}/gates/build.node.sh).
build.node.sh is also the wrong oracle for this project: scripts/resolve.py routes
a repo with tsconfig.json to `gates/build.sh`, and build.node.sh is the plain-JS
gate for repos that have no typechecker. The gate that actually runs here, and the
one the record's own symptom text quotes ("build.sh reported 'tests could not run -
unavailable'"), is the project-local .proof-os/gates/build.sh. Line 44 of the
plugin's build.node.sh and line 15 of build.sh are the same statement,
`TMO="${PROOF_GATE_TIMEOUT:-300}"`, which is presumably how the reference drifted.
Everything below is about .proof-os/gates/build.sh.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. TIMINGS — the budget story does NOT reproduce
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  $ npm test --silent            (solo, nothing else running)
    exit 1, wall 99s
    vitest: Duration 95.56s
            Test Files  1 failed | 106 passed (107)
            Tests       2 failed | 666 passed (668)

  $ bash <HEAD copy of .proof-os/gates/build.sh> "<project>"
    exit 2, wall 159s TOTAL for all three legs (tsc + vite build + vitest)

99s against a 300s budget. 159s for the whole gate. Nothing timed out; `timeout`
never fired; no leg came within 2x of its ceiling.

This also withdraws the justification currently written into build.sh by an
earlier edit, which raised the test budget to 900s citing "a clean solo `npm test`
run completes successfully in ~476s (vitest's own reported Duration: 459.47s)"
and citing THIS log file as its evidence. This log did not exist when that comment
was written, and the number does not reproduce: measured 95.56s, not 459.47s, and
the run does not "complete successfully" — it fails.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2. WHAT ACTUALLY REPRODUCES — every run, and it is worse
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Observed output of the pre-fix gate:

    · tsc --noEmit
    · npm run build
    · npm test
      tests could not run — unavailable
    VERDICT: partial — some oracles could not run (believed, not proved)
    exit 2

"tests could not run" is the ENVIRONMENT branch, not the timeout branch. The
suite had in fact run to completion and FAILED. The gate's env_issue() is

    grep -qiE 'ENOENT|Cannot find module|ERR_MODULE_NOT_FOUND|command not found|
               not recognized|EACCES|ENOSPC|network|ETIMEDOUT|registry\.npmjs'

matched against the ENTIRE test output. Counted over the captured run, exactly one
of those tokens is present, and it is the bare word `network`:

    npmtest_solo.log:169   Failed to refresh deal deal_1 Error: network down
    npmtest_solo.log:1782  Failed to load workspace information Error: network down

Those lines are printed by suites that deliberately exercise a failed fetch. They
appear whether those tests pass or fail. So the test leg has been converted to
`unavailable` on every single run, in both directions, for as long as any test in
this repo has asserted on a network failure.

That is why "this gate has never once returned green": it has never returned any
verdict about tests at all. And the failure mode is not a lost green — it is a RED
SUITE LAUNDERED INTO `unavailable`. Two genuinely failing tests
(src/components/brand/deal-room/__tests__/demo-sign-flow-alive.test.tsx, the
F-0272 control cases) were reported as "the tool could not run".

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
3. WHAT DOES NOT REPRODUCE, AND IS STILL REAL
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The contention the record describes (a subagent running vitest at the same time)
was not the cause today, but nothing in the gate prevents it either: two agents
can still start vitest simultaneously and starve each other. Not reproduced as the
cause; addressed anyway, by serialising rather than by raising a number.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
4. rc / liveness
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The pre-fix project build.sh sources nothing and writes no rc file.
.proof-os/rc/build.rc was untouched by the run above (still
`exit=1 pid=1681 ended=2026-08-17T15:08:20Z`, written by the plugin's copy the day
before). gates/liveness.py therefore could not tell whether this gate had run,
hung, or died.
